/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict --- ED09 tartaric stabilisation of a wine carried as THIRTEEN
  IONS, on a CONDUCTIVITY target
  ===========================================================================

  WHAT THIS CASE IS, AND WHAT ed08 IS NOT.  ed08_wine_kht_model_solution
  reduces the wine to its stability-determining salt, KHT, because on ONE
  1:1 salt the old Faraday transfer (every counter-ion given the WHOLE
  current, xi I N/(|z| F)) was exact.  On a real wine it was not: the
  parked 2026-09-19 attempt at this case removed H+, Cl-, HMal- and Mal 2-
  ENTIRELY while K+ fell 6 %, and left the diluate carrying net charge
  (DEV.md C4).  Vitor ruled the missing rule on 2026-10-05 (C35): the
  counter-ions of each membrane SHARE its current by

      t_i = |z_i| D_i c_i / SUM_j |z_j| D_j c_j       (no new parameter)

  -- the transport numbers of Geraldes & Afonso, J. Membr. Sci. 360 (2010)
  499-508, Eqs. (12)/(13), applied at every current -- integrated along the
  pass, with D_i each ion's D0.  Each membrane then moves exactly
  xi I N / F equivalents and the diluate leaves electroneutral.  This case
  is the full wine that rule unblocks.

  1. ETHANOL IS NOT IN THIS WINE, AND THAT IS THE FIRST THING TO KNOW.  A
  dry red carries about 13 % v/v of ethanol and the stack cannot be told
  so: every non-water component passes through the aqueous-species bridge,
  and declaring `ethanol` in the components list REFUSES -- measured on a
  twin of this case on 2026-10-05: "aqueousMapping: component 'ethanol'
  declares no aqueous mapping", exit 2.  So the engine prices the solvent
  as PURE WATER: Re and Sc on water's viscosity, every ion's conductivity
  on its infinite-dilution D0 in water.  Mobilities scale with 1/viscosity,
  and a water-ethanol mixture is more viscous than water, so kappa_in and
  kappa_out are both overestimated by a common factor this case cannot
  compute; the RELATIVE target (20 %) is insensitive to it, the absolute
  voltage and power are not.  NAMED AND NOT BUILT: a neutral co-solvent
  carried through the mass balance and priced into the solvent viscosity
  and dielectric constant (DEV.md C4 (b)).

  2. THE WINE IS AN AUTHOR-SET COMPOSITION, closed on sulfate -- the table,
  the closure and what it stands for are in 0/diluateFeed.  No number in
  it is transcribed from a measured wine and no source is cited for it; it
  is a round thirteen-ion composition of the order a dry red at pH about
  3.6 carries, chosen so that the stack meets a wine's real spread of
  mobilities: H+ (D0 9.31e-9 m2/s) beside K+ (1.96e-9) beside Mg2+ (0.71e-9)
  on the cation membrane, Cl- (2.03e-9) beside six organic and inorganic
  anions on the anion membrane.  The speciation is FIXED as declared: the
  stack does not speciate, so the H+ it removes is not replaced by the
  undissociated acids a real wine would re-dissociate (DEV.md C4 (d)).

  3. SIX DIFFUSIVITIES ARE ESTIMATES, AND THE RUN SAYS SO SIX TIMES.  K, Na,
  Ca, Mg, H, Cl and SO4 carry curated D0 in the catalogue; HTart, Tart,
  H2PO4, HMal, Mal and Lactate are supplied CASE-LOCALLY under
  constant/species/, each `origin estimated; reviewStatus unverified;` with
  its derivation in the record (a Stokes-Einstein radius from the KHT
  crystal volume, scaled by molar mass; H2PO4- set equal to sulfate) and
  ANNOUNCED on every run.  With the C35 rule these numbers now SET the
  split -- the bitartrate's estimated D0 decides how much of the anion
  current it carries -- so they matter more here than in ed08.

  4. THE TARGET IS CONDUCTIVITY, BECAUSE THAT IS WHAT IS MEASURED (Vitor:
  "na eletrodialise aponta para a condutividade, porque isso e que e
  medido").  `targetConductivityRemoval 0.20;` asks for 20 % of the
  diluate's conductivity removed -- an AUTHOR-SET operating point, the same
  one ed08 uses -- and Choupo solves the current.  The conductivity counts
  every ion with its own z^2 D0 c, so the target does not depend on the
  order of the components list.  T = 298.15 K, as in ed08 and for ed08's
  reason (at 25 C the conductivity and the limiting current read the same
  diffusivities; DEV.md C4 (f)).

  WHAT THE RUN PRINTS (every number is this model's; the golden pins it):

      I = 6.710 A on 0.5 m2 per cell pair (i = 13.4 A/m2), U = 11.40 V,
      P = 76 W, 0.0255 kWh per m3 of wine; kappa 0.4789 -> 0.3831 S/m;
      i_lim = 225.2 A/m2, set by the ANION membrane, so i/i_lim = 0.060.

      ion       membrane   share of its      removed
                           membrane's current
      K+        CEM        0.746             22.4 %
      Na+       CEM        0.105             15.8 %
      Ca2+      CEM        0.032              9.7 %
      Mg2+      CEM        0.093              8.7 %
      H+        CEM        0.023             70.0 %
      Cl-       AEM        0.051             35.1 %
      SO4 2-    AEM        0.324             20.2 %
      HTart-    AEM        0.159             14.9 %
      Tart 2-   AEM        0.059             14.9 %
      HMal-     AEM        0.021             15.4 %
      Mal 2-    AEM        0.002             15.5 %
      Lactate-  AEM        0.209             17.4 %
      H2PO4-    AEM        0.175             20.2 %

  THE LESSON IS IN THE LAST COLUMN.  The fraction of an ion removed
  depends on its D0 ALONE -- ln(1 - removed) / D0 is one number on each
  membrane -- so ions of equal D0 leave in equal FRACTION whatever their
  charge or concentration (HTart- and Tart 2-, which share an estimated D0;
  SO4 2- and H2PO4-, which share one by construction), the fast H+ and Cl-
  are stripped hardest, and the slow divalent cations least.  The SHARE of
  the current, on the other hand, is set by z D c: potassium, the
  dominant cation, carries three quarters of the cation current.  The
  equivalents moved through the two membranes are printed beside the
  table and are equal.

  WHAT IS PINNED AND WHAT IS NOT.  The golden pins this model's answer.
  Nothing here is validated against a measured wine or a measured stack
  run: the composition is author-set, six D0 are announced estimates, the
  sulfate is a closure, the solvent is water, the speciation is frozen, and
  the share z D c is a RULING that leaves out any selectivity the real
  membranes add between counter-ions.  Whether 20 % of the conductivity
  removes enough KHT to stabilise the wine is NOT computed: that needs a
  KHT solubility in a hydroalcoholic medium (DEV.md C4 (e)), which the tree
  does not carry.

      diluateFeed (the wine) ->  +-----------------------+ -> diluate (stabilised wine)
                                 | EurodiaED-100P-50     |
      concentrateFeed (brine) -> | 100 pairs, CMX/AMX    | -> concentrate
                                 +-----------------------+
                                          | (power, energy wire)
                                          v
                                     rectifier (electricLoad)
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        edStack;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( diluateFeed  concentrateFeed );
        outputs     ( diluate  concentrate );

        operation
        {
            stack                      EurodiaED-100P-50;
            membrane                   CMX_AMX;
            targetConductivityRemoval  0.20;
            xi                         0.9;
            E_electrodes               2.0;
        }

        energyOutputs
        (
            { name power;  kind work;  expression "W_electric";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        rectifier;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 1.0; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from edStack.power;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
);
